From cbecdcfc31245c2df538e1fc0d397877be99f63d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 22:21:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/13] evdi: sync with the safe in-tree driver

Refresh the standalone module from the drm-next source of truth. Use the safe DRM registration lifetime, USB device notifier and topology APIs, typed userspace-copy helpers, and the current KMS and DDC/CI interfaces while retaining DisplayLinkManager ABI compatibility.

The synced Rust consumer contains no unsafe blocks or direct bindgen access.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-0
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
